hydroelectric, geothermal, nuclear and other plants) with a total net installed capacity of 80.8 GW as of 30 September 2024, compared to 81.4 GW as of 31 December 2023. For the nine months ended 30 September 2024, net electricity production was 147.2 TWh and distribution of electricity was 363.3 TWh, respectively, compared to 158.3 TWh and 369.2 TWh as of 30 September 2023. The ENEL Group is deeply committed to the renewable energies sector and to researching and developing new environmentally friendly technologies. In 2015, approximately half of the electricity the ENEL Group produced was free of carbon dioxide emissions, ma king it one of the world’s major producers of clean energy. Further, ENEL is committed to becoming a decarbonised company by 2050. In 2016, ENEL’s renewable energy business, operated through by Enel Green Power S.p.A. (“ EGP”) and its subsidiaries, has been the subject matter of a corporate reorganisation with the aim of, inter alia, innovating in renewables at scale and with greater speed. Moreover, ENEL is the first utility in the world to replace conventional electromechanical meters with so-called “smart meters”, being modern electronic meters that enable consumption levels to be read in real time and contracts to be managed remotely. As of the date of this Base Prospectus, ENEL has installed approximately 45.8 million smart meters. This innovative measurement system is essential to the development of smart grids, smart cities and electric mobility. The following tables set forth the Group’s key operating data of the electricity business as of and for the nine months ended 30 September 2024 and 30 September 2023 and as of and for the years ended 31 December 2023 and 2022. 153 Nine months ended 30 September 2024 Nine months ended 30 September 2023 Italy Abroad Total Italy Abroad Total Net electricity production (TWh) .................................................... .................................................... 27.0 120.3 147.2 33.